T Cube corner: three axes at one node
# A connector is a plane, so one of them can never hold rods along x, y and z. Two 3D connectors
# sharing a centre, planes at 90 degrees, can. This is the only way to turn a corner in all three axes.
! the node
C N1 B7 0,0,0 z x
C N2 B7 0,0,0 y z
! one rod down each axis
C X W8 2,0,0
C Y W8 0,2,0
C Z W8 0,0,2
R N1 X
R N1 Y
R N2 Z
